    "updated_at": "2020-06-02T13:00:45Z",
    "body": "See #513 and #518 for some upcoming changes in this area. They don't really change the status quo, but do add percent-encode sets that include U+0025, including one that is an exact match for the one in JavaScript.\r\n\r\nAnd I guess we could add a note that it really depends on the caller which of the various percent-encode sets is safe to use.",
